ed file: 954576cdf45988bd1bab01e2601b852313d3c798a77e776f378d76e9e7a4cd0c\nLocation: 24 FR 3179, PDF pages 1-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 40 ===\n. ^ D N A U * .\nFEDERA\nVOLUME 24 1934\n, Ü N l T t O ^\nWashington, Friday, Aprii 24, 1959\nNUMBER 80\nTitle 3— THE PRESIDENT\nExecutive Order 10810\nREGULATIONS GOVERNING THE AL­\nLOWANCE OF TRAVEL EXPENSES \nOF CLAIMANTS AND BENEFICIAR­\nIES  OF THE VETERANS’ ADMINIS­\nTRATION AND THEIR ATTENDANTS\nS ec. 3. Whenever a claimant or bene­\nficiary requires an attendant other than  \nan employee of the Veterans’  Adminis­\ntration for the performance of travel  \nspecified in sections 1 and 2 hereof, the  \ntravel expenses of such attendant may  \nbe allowed in the same manner and to  \nthe same extent that travel expenses  \nare allowed to such claimant or  \nbeneficiary.\nBy virtue of the authority vested in  \nm e by section 111 of title 38 of the United \nStates Code, I hereby prescribe the fol­\nlow ing regulations governing the allow­\nan ce of travel expenses of claimants and \nbeneficiaries of the Veterans’  Adminis­\ntration and their attendants:\nSection L The Administrator of Vet­\nerans’  Affairs may author","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_10811.txt","sha256":"dee0d477ebbc5683673d4a442f52825e0f6c6e37ed81085a4f32923c17bff4e1","source":{"line":917,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6a012cb463ca0e1c6bb927e958afc9a4ccd0327449ccf0cf6e1eba0b8bc9e461"}}]}
